8,east,"The goal is to reach the stairs down, which is not directly visible but is mentioned as adjacent to the west. Since I am currently in the northwest part of the map and there is no path to the west, I need to explore the east and then make my way back to the west.

First, I will search the current room to see if there are any hidden doors or passages. If there are, I will try to open them to progress.

If there are no hidden doors, I will try to open the horizontal closed door near northnorthwest. If it is locked, I will try to kick it.

Once I have opened a door, I will make my way east to explore the east part of the map. I will try to search the rooms I visit to see if there are any hidden doors or passages.

As I explore the east part of the map, I will keep an eye out for a path that leads west. When I find one, I will make my way back to the stairs down, which should be adjacent to the west.

If I encounter any enemies, I will try to avoid them by running away. If that's not possible, I will use my +1 dagger to defend myself.

My high-level plan is to explore the east part of the map, find a path west, and make my way back to the stairs down.","message:


